# Error Handling Standards

- Always use try-catch blocks in service functions
- Use the error-handling service for consistent error messaging
- Log errors with proper context for easier debugging
- Return meaningful error messages to the UI layer
- Handle Firebase-specific errors with the handleFirebaseError utility

## Error Handling Pattern

```typescript
import { logError, handleFirebaseError } from '@/services/error-handling';

export const someServiceFunction = async (params) => {
  try {
    // Function implementation
    return { success: true, data };
  } catch (error) {
    const errorMessage = handleFirebaseError(error.code) || 'Default error message';
    logError(error, 'someServiceFunction', { params });
    return { success: false, error: errorMessage };
  }
};
```
